title: Walk_Heim_Berkeley
tags: walk
speaker: Heim
---
Heim: We are walking across the Metaphysics grove toward Bishop Berkeley's clearing.
Heim: You have considered my virtual realism and the reality of digital code.
Heim: Sunlight flickers through green branches as we follow this dirt path.
Heim: We move from software structures to idealist philosophy of perception.
Heim: George Berkeley waits in the sunlit clearing just ahead.
Heim: He famously declared that to be is to be perceived.
Heim: He will ask whether a tree in the quad exists when no one looks.
Heim: Consider whether digital objects depend on display screens or minds to exist.
Heim: Compare his idealism with my claim that digital data persists independently.
Heim: Step into his clearing and prepare for his idealist challenge.
===
